<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mozambique Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a> Island is a small coral island off the northern coast of Mozambique, once a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> trading town ruled by a sheikh. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasco-da-gama">Vasco da Gama</a> called there in 1498, and the Portuguese built the Fortress of São Sebastião and made it the capital of Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a> until 1898. It traded and fought with the neighbouring Swahili sheikhdoms and sultanates of Angoche, Sancul and Quitangonha. It is a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mozambique-island.jpg" alt="Mozambique Island" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stig Nygaard from Copenhagen, Denmark · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ilha_de_Mocambique.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
